

                                                        
# Day 3 - AWS Console and IAM Basics

## AWS Management Console

AWS Management Console is a web-based interface used to access and manage AWS services.

Important parts of the AWS Console:

- Search Bar - Used to quickly find AWS services.
- Region Selector - Used to select an AWS Region.
- Services - Provides access to services such as EC2, S3, IAM, VPC, and CloudWatch.
- Account Menu - Used for account-related settings and access.

The AWS Console works as a control panel for managing AWS resources.

## IAM

IAM stands for Identity and Access Management.

IAM is used to control who can access AWS resources and what actions they are allowed to perform.

## IAM User

An IAM User is an individual identity inside an AWS Account.

Example:

AWS Account
    |
IAM User
    |
Permissions
    |
AWS Resources

An IAM User can be given specific permissions according to the user's requirements.

## IAM Group

An IAM Group is a collection of IAM Users.

Example:

Developers Group
    |
    |-- User A
    |-- User B
    |-- User C

Groups are useful when multiple users require common permissions.

User = Individual identity

Group = Collection of users

## IAM Policy

An IAM Policy is a permission rule or document that defines what an identity is allowed or denied to do.

Basic structure:

User / Group
    |
Policy
    |
Permissions
    |
AWS Resource

Important policy concepts:

- Effect - Defines whether an action is Allow or Deny.
- Action - Defines what action can be performed.
- Resource - Defines which AWS resource the action applies to.

Example:

Developer
    |
S3 Read Permission - Allowed
S3 Delete Permission - Not Allowed

## Least Privilege

Least Privilege means giving an identity only the permissions required to perform its specific task.

Example:

If a developer only needs to read files from S3, the developer should receive S3 read permission instead of unnecessary administrator permissions.

Simple rule:

Give only the access that is actually required.


